      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EASTCOAST HUSSLER (8) is the horse to beat despite missing as favourite at Prairie last start, with his broader profile still very appealing for a Benchmark 62. He has won three of seven, drops from 62.5kg to 58kg, and his Blackall win over 1400m as a well-supported favourite reads strongly enough for this. LONERGY (3) brings the most reliable recent finishing form, coming out of a provincial Dalby second where he was hampered on the home turn and still finished within just under two lengths of Hello Dolly Diva. TOO MANY KISSES (9) is race fit, backs up quickly, and returns to Emerald after a Benchmark 55 win here before a sound Class 3 second at Thangool. LUNAR EIGHT (4) is the consistent danger, beaten only a neck last start after winning a Class 3 on soft ground two back, but she may need to produce her best again at this trip.",
